      <dataObjectReference id="dataObjectReference_0d447ecc-e24d-4886-becf-d03f9d718b5e"
                            name="Existing settlement instructions and statuses"
                            dataObjectRef="_0d447ecc-e24d-4886-becf-d03f9d718b5e">
         <documentation id="documentation_0d447ecc-e24d-4886-becf-d03f9d718b5e"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-004; CSP-PR-005; CSP-ST-002; CSP-ST-005; CSP-ST-006.
 
Purpose: Information obtained from SYS-SET about settlement instructions already associated with the reviewed trades.
 
Content: Available instruction identifiers, trade and version references, currency-leg identification, current instruction statuses, and any recorded settlement outcomes or failure reasons.
 
Usage: Settlement Operations checks this information when determining whether a trade requires preparation, monitoring, or exception investigation. Existing instructions and confirmed settled-leg outcomes must be considered before any further submission.
 
Missing or ambiguous instruction information requires investigation and must not be trated as proof that no instruction exists. Overall settlement success requires confirmed settlement of both currency legs.]]></documentation>
